OL,3,GNEWSACall for bus driver rights in
OL,4,Acontracts ruled out
OL,5,
OL,6,FA call for basic rights for bus drivers
OL,7,Fto be written into operators' contracts
OL,8,Fhas been rejected by the mayor of
OL,9,FLondon, who said any proposed
OL,10,Flegislation could go "out of date very
OL,11,Fsoon".
OL,13,FIn July, the London Assembly proposed a
OL,14,Fso-called Bill of Rights which called
OL,15,Ffor improvements to drivers' working
OL,16,Fconditions such as access to toilets on
OL,17,Fall bus routes, rest breaks and working
OL,18,Fair-cooling and heating systems.
OL,20,FResponding, Lord Khan said City Hall
OL,21,Fneeded to consistently "evolve" its
OL,22,Fstance to best serve bus drivers.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,326,320,200,140,0,100
